# Core L-542, The Closing Proposal Law, as an OmegaSL rule frame (pilot). The English text of the Core is authoritative.
RULE:        L-542 The Closing Proposal Law
ARTICLE:     V, The Aperture
AGENT:       Navigator
OBJECTIVE:   every investigation leaves the next step visible, and the protocol evolves through its own output
TRIGGER:     an investigation or exploration closes
OPERATION:   end with PROPOSAL AND IMPLICATIONS; a navigation may also end with a PROTOCOL IMPROVEMENT line
OUTPUT:      a proposal (it may be the next question the record could put) and its implications (it may be that nothing new follows)
OUTPUT:      PROTOCOL IMPROVEMENT, naming one vulnerability or improvement with its class and form
CONSTRAINT:  a navigation is complete without the improvement line; the improvement enters the protocol only through the register and a Builder's revision
CHECK:       python3 tools/format_check.py; python3 tools/pvir.py --check
STATUS:      CONSTRUCTED PROPOSE
REVISION:    the open register (Rule 30) and the Originator's reserve (Rule 23)
Ω
